509	    41	/**
510	    42	 * This is the main class for creating a map/reduce job using Aggregate
511	    43	 * framework. The Aggregate is a specialization of map/reduce framework,
512	    44	 * specializing for performing various simple aggregations.
513	    45	 * 
514	    46	 * Generally speaking, in order to implement an application using Map/Reduce
515	    47	 * model, the developer is to implement Map and Reduce functions (and possibly
516	    48	 * combine function). However, a lot of applications related to counting and
517	    49	 * statistics computing have very similar characteristics. Aggregate abstracts
518	    50	 * out the general patterns of these functions and implementing those patterns.
519	    51	 * In particular, the package provides generic mapper/redducer/combiner 
520	    52	 * classes, and a set of built-in value aggregators, and a generic utility 
521	    53	 * class that helps user create map/reduce jobs using the generic class. 
522	    54	 * The built-in aggregators include:
523	    55	 * 
524	    56	 * sum over numeric values count the number of distinct values compute the
525	    57	 * histogram of values compute the minimum, maximum, media,average, standard
526	    58	 * deviation of numeric values
527	    59	 * 
528	    60	 * The developer using Aggregate will need only to provide a plugin class
529	    61	 * conforming to the following interface:
530	    62	 * 
531	    63	 * public interface ValueAggregatorDescriptor { public ArrayList&lt;Entry&gt;
532	    64	 * generateKeyValPairs(Object key, Object value); public void
533	    65	 * configure(Configuration conf); }
534	    66	 * 
535	    67	 * The package also provides a base class, ValueAggregatorBaseDescriptor,
536	    68	 * implementing the above interface. The user can extend the base class and
537	    69	 * implement generateKeyValPairs accordingly.
538	    70	 * 
539	    71	 * The primary work of generateKeyValPairs is to emit one or more key/value
540	    72	 * pairs based on the input key/value pair. The key in an output key/value pair
541	    73	 * encode two pieces of information: aggregation type and aggregation id. The
542	    74	 * value will be aggregated onto the aggregation id according the aggregation
543	    75	 * type.
544	    76	 * 
545	    77	 * This class offers a function to generate a map/reduce job using Aggregate
546	    78	 * framework. The function takes the following parameters: input directory spec
547	    79	 * input format (text or sequence file) output directory a file specifying the
548	    80	 * user plugin class
549	    81	 * 
550	    82	 */
